    "blurb": "Sovereign Camunda deployment on STACKIT",
    "overview": "Consid designs and builds Camunda Self-Managed on STACKIT, the sovereign cloud of the Schwarz Group. Delivered entirely as Terraform, Helm and GitOps in your Git, production-ready in weeks, with data staying in Germany.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Deploy sovereign process orchestration, delivered entirely as code",
    "splashDescription": "Many European organizations need to run Camunda where EU law applies, with process data, backups and logs staying in the EU and meeting GDPR requirements by design. This professional service from Consid deploys Camunda Self-Managed onto STACKIT, the sovereign cloud of the Schwarz Group, giving every stateful Camunda component, including Zeebe, Operate, Tasklist, Identity and Web Modeler, a managed STACKIT counterpart, from multi-AZ Kubernetes and PostgreSQL to OpenSearch, S3-compatible object storage, observability and secrets management, all operated in German data centers under German jurisdiction. Consid delivers the entire platform as code, using the STACKIT Terraform provider, Helm and GitOps, so every environment is reproducible and version controlled in your own Git repository, and you own the platform instead of depending on hand-built infrastructure or proprietary tooling. Delivery starts with an assessment of your process landscape and compliance constraints, then Consid engineers embed with your team to provision the platform, wire up SSO, connectors and CI/CD, and hand over runbooks and rehearsed backup and restore, typically reaching a first production cluster within two to three weeks of kickoff. Consid is a Swedish digital transformation consultancy founded in 2000, with more than 1,800 experts across 45-plus offices in six countries, bringing Camunda process expertise, Kubernetes platform engineering and STACKIT know-how together under one roadmap and one escalation path.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/844739/overview/img7121003613133564382.png?de91b279644eb8ba35c5aec2244c471f",
